  "description": "ENENOC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H92 Dy8 N24 O32,2(C2 H3 N1),10(C1 H4 O1),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.638-4.555 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.14-138.31°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C118H150Dy8N26O48. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
